## Errors & Mistakes
No failed commands, but the subagent launch was wrong and cost a round trip.
I passed prompts via the Agent tool's `prompt` field with run_in_background
false. The agents spawned as NAMED BACKGROUND TEAMMATES that ignored the prompt
and sat idle, returning only idle_notification with idleReason "available". The
spawn result said "will receive instructions via mailbox," which is the tell.
I had to re-send every task via SendMessage. If you spawn named agents in this
harness, assume the prompt is not the task and send it through SendMessage.

reviewer-semantics also sent its full report twice, the second time labelled
a resend claiming the first "may not have been delivered." It had been. Do not
re-adjudicate a resend; diff it and move on.

