The single most useful analytical result was not a contradiction. It was that
subtractive-engineering.md:18 and :64 delegate exactly five topics to
simple.md — explicit data, isolated state, reduced coupling, clarity over
cleverness, delayed abstraction — leaving Say No by Default, Prototype First,
Design for Failure, Testing Strategy, API Design, and Chesterton's Fence
UNDELEGATED. Every genuine conflict lives in the undelegated six; delegated
topics compose by construction. Two reviewers reached this independently. Use
it to triage any future claim of conflict between these files before spending
effort on it.

That test refuted three findings that four reviewers had rated HARD
CONTRADICTION: logging at simple.md:92 (under "### Code Clarity Over
Cleverness"), boundary validation at :66 (under "### Explicit Data & Isolated
State"), and third-use extraction (under "### Delay Abstraction"). Majority
vote across critics is not evidence; check the section heading.

## Codebase Discoveries
~/.claude/rules is a SYMLINK to /Users/abatilo/abatilo/vimrc/rules, so these
edits changed Aaron's live global context the moment they were written, before
the commit. No install step, and no way to stage a rules change for review
without it being live.

rules/ sits outside plugins/abatilo-core, so the MANDATORY version bump in
plugins/abatilo-core/CLAUDE.md does not apply to this commit. It did apply to
919c801, which removed a skill.

The two files' cross-referencing is one-directional: subtractive-engineering.md
names rules/simple.md twice, simple.md never names subtractive-engineering.md.
That asymmetry is why the precedence defect had no textual resolution.

